 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+Open `/devtools-times/account` from the header. Password sign-in is verified by
+our existing remote login service and creates a local, HTTP-only Astro session.
+Readers can register passkeys, rename their account labels, change their account
+display name, remove credentials, and sign in with a registered passkey.
+Registration and authentication verify the challenge, origin, RP ID, and user
+verification on the server. Account sessions expire after 24 hours.
+
+Account records default to `.data/accounts`. Set `ACCOUNT_DATA_DIR` to a private,
+persistent directory when deploying. The file store serializes writes within a
+single Node process; deployments with multiple instances need a shared database
+with transactional updates and a shared Astro session driver. Local ephemeral
+storage will lose passkey registrations on instance replacement. Credentials are
+scoped to the exact hostname where they were registered.
+
+The WebAuthn Signal API sends the complete accepted credential list and account
+name after loading or saving settings. Passkey labels are local to the account;
+the account display name updates the authenticator's user details. Unsupported
+browsers or rejected signals show instructions for manual password-manager
+updates. A sync failure does not roll back a completed account change.
+
+Run `node --test tests/*.test.ts` on Node 24+ for storage, request protection, and
+browser sync unit tests, and `pnpm run build` for a production build.
